Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS — Enable content editors using Contentstack CMS to see a live, real-time preview of how their content changes render on the GO, UP, and MX sites as they edit.

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. The `options` object passed to `contentstack.Stack()` is missing the `live_preview` configuration required for Contentstack Live Preview to function. Without enabling live preview at the SDK initialization level, no downstream component can receive real-time content updates, regardless of any provider or hook changes.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a `live_preview` property to the `options` object before it is passed to `contentstack.Stack()`. The property should include `enable: true`, `host` (from a new env var e.g. CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST), and `port` if applicable. Also add the corresponding env var destructuring alongside the existing CONTENTSTACK_* vars at lines 17-24. This is the Contentstack SDK's documented entry point for live preview — the Stack must be created with live_preview enabled or the SDK will not emit preview events. After this, `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx` ContentstackProvider must subscribe to Stack live preview callbacks (e.g. `Stack.onEntryChange`) to update the `content` value in context, replacing the current static `useMemo` over `defaultContent`.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a content editor modifies a field of a published entry in Contentstack and views the GO site in Live Preview, the rendered page displays the newly edited value in place of the old one without a redeploy or rebuild.
- When a content editor modifies a field of a published entry in Contentstack and views the UP site in Live Preview, the rendered page displays the newly edited value in place of the old one without a redeploy or rebuild.
- When a content editor modifies a field of a published entry in Contentstack and views the MX site in Live Preview, the rendered page displays the newly edited value in place of the old one without a redeploy or rebuild.
- When a page on the GO, UP, or MX site is opened in Live Preview mode, the page renders fully with its published content visible, including header, body, and footer regions.
- When a content editor opens Live Preview for an entry whose draft contains empty or invalid fields, the GO, UP, and MX site pages render completely and remain interactive, displaying the last valid content for those fields.

